        "22": {
            "type": "markdown",
            "content": "**Burn-rate alert setup**\n1. Create a metric event from DQL instead of using a static threshold.\n2. Calculate each SLI over a short and a long window, then convert failures to burn rate using budget = 100 - target.\n3. Use the highest burn among availability, errors, and latency as the paging signal.\n4. Route notifications from the alerting profile to email, Slack, or workflow automation.\n\n**Suggested thresholds for a 30-day SLO**\n- Page: burn rate > 14 over 1h and > 6 over 6h\n- Ticket: burn rate > 3 over 1d and > 1 over 3d\n\n**Composite DQL pattern**\n- availability burn = (100 - availability_sli) / 0.05\n- error burn = (100 - error_free_sli) / 0.5\n- latency burn = (100 - latency_sli) / 5\n- composite burn = max of the three burns"
        },
